    {
        "content": "<p>The proof itself is not hard, but we also need to fix the downstream usage.</p>",
        "id": 617051356,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhenhua Wu",
        "timestamp": 1787001871
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also the mathlib community might want you to generalise those result.</p>",
        "id": 617051570,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhenhua Wu",
        "timestamp": 1787001964
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hey isn't this just the theorem that any setoid satisfying <code>hmul</code> is the cosets of some subgroup</p>",
        "id": 617052202,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1787002253
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah it doesn't really need to the topological parts on the end. So maybe we should check if such result live in the Group file, and state a corollary in Topology-Algebra file.</p>",
        "id": 617053362,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhenhua Wu",
        "timestamp": 1787002783
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>To my mind, the equivalence relation on a topological algebraic structure should be determined by topological properties.</p>",
        "id": 617053545,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhenhua Wu",
        "timestamp": 1787002855
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, we should abstract the theorem about irreducible component of unit in a topological group is a normal subgroup. It is a different path of a proof, because the collection of irreducible components are not a partition or equivalence relation.</p>",
        "id": 617053785,
        "sender_full_name": "Zhenhua Wu",
        "timestamp": 1787002979
    }
]